  "description": "All that You Need to Know About Solidworks If you are someone who loves designing or dreams of innovating an out-of-the-box utility one day, then this is the place for you. SOLIDWORKS aims to test the design and imaginative capability of the contestant. This is a platform where the participant can show off all their CAD skills. The participant will be required to create a 3D model of a given problem statement in the allotted time. Guidelines: Time Allocated: 2 hours. Round 2 will be followed by a 10-minute explanation session with judges where the participants will have to explain the approach to the part/assembly modeled and will be judged accordingly. Participants will be evaluated based on: Number of parts successfully modeled and assembled. Constraining of parts in the assembly. Whether sub-assemblies were used and why. Appropriateness of the constraints used for assembly. Participants must create a Word/PDF file illustrating different views of the assembly, exploded views of the assembly, dimensions, and work history (timeline) and save the files (Sldprt/Sldasm files) with the proper name format for submission. Submission Guidelines: Participants are supposed to submit the following files: Word/PDF file. SolidWorks file (Sldprt/Sldasm). Files should have the following name format for submission: Qno_Team-name_round (e.g., Q2_alpha_round1.pdf and Q1_alpha_round2.sldprt, where \"alpha\" is the team name). Participating teams have to mail their files (Word/PDF and SolidWorks files) in a single mail. Rules: Any misbehavior of a participant during the event/rounds may lead to disqualification. Absent participants will be automatically disqualified. All the rights are reserved with the Event Organizer Committee. In case of any disputes, the final wording will remain with the organizers. The decision of the judges is final. Only entries submitted within the specified deadline will be considered for evaluation. Link for the meet will be provided via email. Team Size: 1",
