    "details": "<p class=\"blue_un-border-before hdng mock-title\"><strong>All that You Need to Know About Solidworks</strong></p>\n<div class=\"position-relative\">\n<div class=\"blue_un-border-before comp-detail un_editor_text_live expanded\">\n<p>If you are someone who loves designing or dreams of innovating an out-of-the-box utility one day, then this is the place for you.</p>\n<p><strong>SOLIDWORKS</strong> aims to test the design and imaginative capability of the contestant. This is a platform where the participant can show off all their CAD skills. The participant will be required to create a 3D model of a given problem statement in the allotted time.</p>\n<p><strong>Guidelines:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Time Allocated:</strong>&nbsp;2 hours.</li>\n<li><strong>Round 2 will be followed by a 10-minute </strong>explanation session with judges where the participants will have to explain the approach to the part/assembly modeled and will be judged accordingly.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Participants will be evaluated based on:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Number of parts successfully modeled and assembled.</li>\n<li>Constraining of parts in the assembly.</li>\n<li>Whether sub-assemblies were used and why.</li>\n<li>Appropriateness of the constraints used for assembly.</li>\n<li>Participants must create a Word/PDF file illustrating different views of the assembly, exploded views of the assembly, dimensions, and work history (timeline) and save the files (Sldprt/Sldasm files) with the proper name format for submission.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Submission Guidelines:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Participants are supposed to submit the following files:\n<ul>\n<li>Word/PDF file.</li>\n<li>SolidWorks file (Sldprt/Sldasm).</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>Files should have the following name format for submission:\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Qno_Team-name_round</strong>&nbsp;(e.g., Q2_alpha_round1.pdf and Q1_alpha_round2.sldprt, where \"alpha\" is the team name).</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>Participating teams have to mail their files (Word/PDF and SolidWorks files) in a single mail.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Rules:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Any misbehavior of a participant during the event/rounds may lead to disqualification.</li>\n<li>Absent participants will be automatically disqualified.</li>\n<li>All the rights are reserved with the Event Organizer Committee.</li>\n<li>In case of any disputes, the final wording will remain with the organizers. The decision of the judges is final.</li>\n<li>Only entries submitted within the specified deadline will be considered for evaluation.</li>\n<li>Link for the meet will be provided via email.</li>\n<li><strong>Team Size:</strong>&nbsp;1</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n</div>",
    "end_date": "2027-03-04T19:00:00+05:30",
